From 9ddff75045a2147ebcc4195ca09d02fc32c7a919 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajensenwaud <ajensenwaud@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 20:53:31 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 02/26] ling: the #874 family on v1.2.0's GLM kernels, lanes
 ABI and host package; EXL3 through main's shared operators
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Port of the previous commit onto v1.2.0:
- main's ling host package wins (config, names, synth and their tests); the family reads Config.groups() and
  layerLimits() from it.
- Ling's kernels are new tf_ling_* entries of GLM's glue image, templated off GLM's device code so every
  tf_glm_* entry instantiates the old parameters: absorb_q/expand_v at 128-wide heads, GPT-J rope over the
  64 roped columns, the chunked attention 576 wide (16-head blocks), group-limited top-k (8 groups keep 4).
  Their launches sit in ling/ops.zig; GLM's API gains only cuda_latent.merge as pub.
- experts.zig keeps v1.2.0's layout; Layer.after selects the FP8 experts' EPI 4 instances (Ling's clamp
  order). NVFP4 has no such instance on main: a clamped NVFP4 layer is refused.
- lanes backend: prefill_step's row cap (new ABI) taken and ignored; the fake driver answers the VMM attributes.
- tests/cuda: Ling's commands in ling_cmds.zig, wired from main.zig; checks of GLM's old fatbin bytes dropped
  (main's GLM kernels are unchanged, proved by SASS identity instead).
EXL3 (exllamav3 packs): config admits quant_method exl3 (mul1, mcg, 3inst codebooks); every quantized
linear is main's exl3.Weight on qlinear's exl3 arm (cuda.exl3.Dense), the fused qkv_proj as three column
views, kv_a_proj_with_mqa at its stored 640 columns (read past the padding); routed experts as main's
exl3_experts.Layer through exl3_grouped; unquantized fp16 tensors rounded to bf16. Clamped EXL3 expert
layers are refused until the shared EXL3 epilogue has Ling's clamp order.
ling-exl3-layers: real layers on exllamav3's inputs, prompt and decode, outputs saved for the parity script.

Co-authored-by: Jürgen Schmied <600316+jschmied@users.noreply.github.com>
